{
  "description": "Load order divider paks, recognised by UUID so section boundaries are exact on import and insertable on export.",
  "source": "Astra's Load Order Dividers",
  "credit": "Made by Astralities, used with permission.",
  "creditUrl": "https://forums.nexusmods.com/profile/106303673-astralities/",
  "prefixNote": "Pak filename prefixes that identify a divider set. A UUID is exact but not durable: an author who rebuilds their set issues new ones, and Keileon told us theirs will change because the project folders are gone. A filename prefix is the identifier an author can promise across a rebuild, and it is the only signal that survives both new UUIDs and restyled labels. Matched case-insensitively against the pak filename and the folder, and only ever used to classify a row as a divider rather than to place it.",
